{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_e6b3dca7d4894ea1f742f4e16290fa1494ca4202c67c3c0276424e04379522ff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the project adopts a Contributor Covenant v2.0 code of conduct defining acceptable behavior, an enforcement ladder (warning through permanent ban), and reporting via the maintainer's Instagram handle."}],"claim_ids":["clm_e6b3dca7d4894ea1f742f4e16290fa1494ca4202c67c3c0276424e04379522ff"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:23:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_b6953eab91c944bba9be2abbe9ef326d","id":"pg_97571aba14af593ea11702daa1853cd6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sr5434-codegebragpt-code-of-conduct-md-780307f4b361-02daa1853cd6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d3d56cc7d84f5cebbbb24e73216ca329"],"title":"sr5434/CodegebraGPT/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @ 780307f4b361","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:23:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_b6953eab91c944bba9be2abbe9ef326d"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1f0afc0379d6f78fead65f4817ce14570c548ab15146850ae9365fe69cf3e71f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README says about 100k samples are used for training (the 100k-text subset) out of roughly one million combined samples, to save costs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3aaa73238993505a6bde83eadb1f8e8b10d075420e2fe3f0d6915f32151ea6c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project's stated purpose is finetuning multimodal LLMs on STEM datasets."},{"claim_ids":["clm_56d0a970385bf2e72ea307271b096d2f3ae552fefbe260ab935956141088821d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"As of this snapshot, dataset compilation/preprocessing is marked complete while finetuning and Hugging Face release remain unchecked, so the model appears not yet trained or released."},{"claim_ids":["clm_70992677d6bcb6e660f2ca5a35654f69fc301bcab847623c7bb40f25b68e659a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned base model for finetuning is upstage/SOLAR-10.7B-Instruct-v1.0, using the QLoRA method."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7d041da455c6625a54a9ea334e3efacb60bd02adc17b636db50ca02c51c24eb2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Training data is drawn from public Hugging Face datasets including MetaMathQA, Camel AI math/chemistry/physics/biology, GSM8K, MMLU, Evol Instruct Code, Glaive code assistant, arXiv-derived instruct sets, and ScienceQA."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c503c7d7cc21d6f8be57e004081ad9a4959b8b0f5123f6f83a094cb126de9bbc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The model is named after the author's earlier Codegebra equation-solving program and is intended as its successor with a more natural interface and expanded abilities."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1f0afc0379d6f78fead65f4817ce14570c548ab15146850ae9365fe69cf3e71f","clm_3aaa73238993505a6bde83eadb1f8e8b10d075420e2fe3f0d6915f32151ea6c7","clm_56d0a970385bf2e72ea307271b096d2f3ae552fefbe260ab935956141088821d","clm_70992677d6bcb6e660f2ca5a35654f69fc301bcab847623c7bb40f25b68e659a","clm_7d041da455c6625a54a9ea334e3efacb60bd02adc1